/110657#issuecomment-3371188465>\r\n>\r\n> The same is happening to me in Godot 4.5.stable and OBS 32.0.1. It only\r\n> happens when using the Game Capture source in OBS, not with the regular\r\n> Window or Screen sources. Flipping the source in OBS is not a good solution\r\n> since it also flips the mouse, so it appears completely out of position and\r\n> visually flipped. You can just use regular Window and Screen capture\r\n> sources, but I think it's a serious bug since it can make unaware content\r\n> creators avoid streaming/recording your game if they don't know how to fix\r\n> it.\r\n>\r\n> —\r\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\r\n> <https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110657#issuecomment-3371188465>,\r\n> or unsubscribe\r\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/AAGDJLLX5YT4Q5J4LYZSCSL3WJHXHAVCNFSM6AAAAACG3VSTUOVHI2DSMVQWIX3LMV43OSLTON2WKQ3PNVWWK3TUHMZTGNZRGE4DQNBWGU>\r\n> .\r\n> You are receiving this because you authored the thread.Message ID:\r\n> ***@***.***>\r\n>\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3371248167/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3372443725","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110657#issuecomment-3372443725","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110657","id":3372443725,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7JA2hN","user":{"login":"sergioabreu-g","id":26823024,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI2ODIzMDI0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26823024?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergioabreu-g","html_url":"https://github.com/sergioabreu-g","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sergioabreu-g/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/use