}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vanhoutk/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vanhoutk/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vanhoutk/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vanhoutk/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vanhoutk/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vanhoutk/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vanhoutk/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-19T17:49:13Z","updated_at":"2025-10-19T17:49:13Z","body":"Have had a few streamers run into this issue with our game demo during NextFest","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3419838366/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3420265167","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/110657#issuecomment-3420265167","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/110657","id":3420265167,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7L3RrP","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-20T02:05:46Z","updated_at":"2025-10-20T02:27:06Z","body":"~@Calinou Can you investigate this a bit? I suspect that OBS is somehow intercepting the final blit and is now reading our internal offscreen render target (i.e. the Viewport) directly instead of reading from the final output to the window. That is a problem for several reasons, but making things upside down is one of them.~\n\n~Hopefully there is a way for us to trick OBS into actually capturing the final window output instead of grabbing the internal render target.~\n\nActually I think I figured this out. I'll make a PR shortly. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3420265167/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]